#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
patch_L322_D_7_gallery_page_reads_served_pole_20260925.py -- L-322 Stage D, gallery patch 2 of 3: the page reads the served
pole and frame rows, and stops typing its own numbers.

Built on gallery d892ed6e8b12ba083ebeaf1fed9c84a9db530582 at
https://github.com/tonylquintanilla/tonyquintanilla.github.io, with
orrery c6cbacaeae5ca3d3e0d2cc5aa20842222aa472e3 at
https://github.com/tonylquintanilla/palomas_orrery.

WHAT IT DOES

    gallery/feature_renderers.js no longer types kilometres per AU or the
    frame's angle. It takes both from frame_constants in the served
    cache, which patch D6 put there. Without kilometres per AU nothing is
    drawn; without the angle no pole is placed. Each missing row is a
    warning in the room's notes, never a remembered number.

    The Earth room draws Earth's pole of date as the cache builder served
    it -- for the axis, the equator, the geostationary ring and the belts
    alike -- and the axis hover prints the served tilt with its date. If
    no pole of date is served, it draws the frame's axis and says so.

    The Sun, Jupiter and Saturn draw as before, and no hover text changed.
    Measured trace by trace against the current page, the largest shift in
    any coordinate is two parts in a hundred million of the drawing's size
    (Jupiter's rings). It comes from the frame's angle now being exactly
    84381.448 arcseconds, where the page had typed it to six decimals of a
    degree -- a difference of 0.0004 arcseconds.

    No cache build is needed. The page reads what the last build served.

FILES

    changed  gallery/feature_renderers.js
    changed  gallery/earth_geometry.js
    changed  interactive.html
    changed  gallery/solar_system_earth_test2.html  (the test page)
    changed  documentation/smoke_features.js, smoke_framing.js,
             smoke_sun_shells.js, smoke_earth_geometry.js,
             smoke_hover_budget.js, smoke_arrival.js,
             smoke_display_figures.js
    new      documentation/fixture_hovers_L322d7_on_d892ed6e.json

    Permanent: all of the above. This script is one-shot; archive it to
    documentation/ once it has run.

RUN COMMAND

    Save this file in the gallery repo root (the folder holding
    interactive.html), open it in VS Code, and click Run.

    Success: one "ok" line per file, then "PATCH APPLIED" and the next
    steps. Failure: "FAILURE: ..." and NOTHING is written. Undo after a
    success is Discard Changes in GitHub Desktop.

Written September 25, 2026 with Anthropic's Claude Opus 5.5.
"""

